{"call": 13, "code": "import numpy as np\ndef equation(t, P, params):\n    k = params[0]\n    e = np.exp(-k*t)\n    # basis per P power: [1, t, t^2, e, t*e, t^2*e]\n    C = np.array([\n        [-7.2425, -0.0303, 0.0010, 7.2342, 3.5569, 0.6322],   # P^0\n        [-0.0320,  0.0061,-0.0003, 0.0399,-0.0061, 0.0152],   # P^1\n        [-0.2272, -0.0034, 0.0002,-0.0225, 0.0022,-0.0081],   # P^2\n        [ 0.0205,  0.0042,-0.0001,-0.0141,-0.0010,-0.0005],   # P^3\n    ])\n    B = [np.ones_like(t), t, t**2, e, t*e, t**2*e]\n    out = np.zeros_like(t, dtype=float) + 0.0*P\n    for j in range(4):\n        out = out + P**j * sum(C[j,i]*B[i] for i in range(6))\n    return out", "train_nmse": 0.003892965857147311, "params": [0.7456252204696979, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5]}
